{"signature": "44634a7fd185c844ab60f5fd67566e825b0cb128594a3471fe1b0871446f5f37", "result": {"checks": {"check": {"scope": {"id": "check", "service": "gdocs", "file": "data.json", "pointer": "/docs_documents", "field": "document_id", "values": ["f_023c7331d7e34900bd226f", "f_744027532fb1b0cc8821c4", "f_80db8860fb69d86887c2c0"]}, "matches": [{"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gdocs/data.json", "pointer": "/docs_documents/4", "field": "document_id", "value": "f_023c7331d7e34900bd226f", "record": {"body_text": "Zombie Lane\nDescription & Mechanics\nTrophy Path is a constant Live-Ops feature that rewards players for achieving certain levels in game play.\nResources\nFigma All UI live here.\nRewards Rewards and introduction order lives here.\nIcon Behaviour\n|  | The icon is displayed on the right corner of the main screen.   The icon is always on top of the list.   The icon displays a red dot, if the player has items to claim within the event.   The progress is visible on the event icon. |\n| --- | --- |\nThe Scene\n|  | The scene is a scrollable object.    It always begins at the last achieved milestone and moves as far as the event allows.   The achieved milestones are shown differently than the unachieved ones.   The map icon takes the player to the last unclaimed reward.  The levels players have not achieved are displayed with a dark gray background (see image below). If that level is passed in the main game, they get a golden shield (see image below)   The \u201ci\u201d button displays an infographic.   \u201cX\u201d button takes the player to the main menu. |\n| --- | --- |\nContainer Logic\nThere are 6 types of containers with different display logic. See backend logic at the bottom of the document for how they translate into UI.\n| CONTAINER 0 | Normal milestones with no rewards are showed as Container 0 in the documentation. |\n| --- | --- |\n| CONTAINER 1 | Displays a single small item. The reward item is in the middle, and the quantity is shown underneath.   The corresponding level is displayed in the bottom left corner of the container.   The bottom right portion of the container displays a \u201cClaim\u201d button if the reward is still unclaimed, and a green tick symbol for the claimed rewards.     Displays 2 small items. Same UI, display and claim button state rules apply |\n| --- | --- |\n| CONTAINER 2 | Displays 3 small items. Same UI, display and claim button state rules apply. |\n| --- | --- |\n| CONTAINER 3 | Displays 4 small items. Same UI, display and claim button state rules apply. |\n| --- | --- |\n| CONTAINER 4 | Displays 1 large item. Same UI, display and claim button state rules apply. |\n| --- | --- |\n| CONTAINER 5 | This container is designated for unlocking. It  displays the unlocked item and a small currency reward.   \u201cI\u201d button displays a pop-up style infographic. (see infographic section for more detail)  Left side displays the \u201cUNLOCK TYPE\u201d item   The right side displays the currency reward and quantity which is nestled at a Reward column prior. |\n| --- | --- |\nReward Claim\nWhen a reward becomes available, the player is informed via a red dot on the screen. The red dot shows the number of rewards available for claim. From There, they can enter the Zombie Lane scene and claim their rewards.\nInfographic Pop-Ups\nInfographic pop-ups are available for certain items via the \u201ci\u201d button.  But we should make the entire panel clickable and will bring up the pop up even if they don\u2019t click on the \u201ci\u201d\n|  | Meet&Greet UI is used to introduce zombies in the event.   It has one header, one funny tagline and and an explanation to her ability at the bottom.   \u201cx\u201d exits to Zombie Lane scene. |\n| --- | --- |\n|  | Unlocked UI is used to display the contents of the item pack.    \u201cx\u201d exits to Zombie Lane scene. |\n| --- | --- |\nData Driving\nThe order of rewards that are displayed in the event will be controlled via an Excel sheet linked in the resources section.\n| step | Displays TRUE or FALSE.  If it\u2019s true it means the level will be displayed on the lane.   For instance, if level 8 is TRUE it\u2019s displayed on the lane like this.     If the step is a reward level, the level information is displayed on the container instead of the gray step. |\n| --- | --- |\n| CONTAINER | If a level has no rewards, meaning it\u2019s just a step, then the container info shows FALSE.  There are 6 container types (see container logic above). If the level has a reward in it, the type of container is displayed here.   For instance level 7 has 2 small rewards which is the  display type of the Container 2. |\n| --- | --- |\n| REWARD & QUANTITY | There are 4 reward and quantity columns because the rewards can go up to 4. The reward tab displays the name of the object, and the quantity displays the number of rewards being given of that object. |\n| --- | --- |\n| UNLOCK & UNLOCK TYPE | Some levels have an unlock column. If the level doesn\u2019t have anything to unlock, it shows FALSE. If this is true, it displays what is being unlocked.   For example if a new zombie is being introduced, the unlock column says \u201cZombie\u201d. Let\u2019s say the Cheerleader zombie is being introduced. Then the UNLOCK TYPE says \u201cCheerleader\u201d |\n| --- | --- |", "created_time": "2025-06-16T16:50:28Z", "document_id": "f_023c7331d7e34900bd226f", "drive_file_id": "f_023c7331d7e34900bd226f", "modified_time": "2025-07-18T17:07:06Z", "owner_email": "julia.lawson@harmonygames.co", "revision_id": "8a2bf1e230", "shared_with_emails": ["frederick.stone@harmonygames.co", "PERSON_2360_EMAIL", "PERSON_3138_EMAIL"], "style_runs": [{"end": 11, "list_id": null, "list_nesting": 0, "named_style": "TITLE", "start": 0}, {"end": 35, "list_id": null, "list_nesting": 0, "named_style": "HEADING_1", "start": 12}, {"end": 152, "list_id": null, "list_nesting": 0, "named_style": "HEADING_1", "start": 143}, {"end": 242, "list_id": null, "list_nesting": 0, "named_style": "HEADING_1", "start": 228}, {"end": 503, "list_id": null, "list_nesting": 0, "named_style": "HEADING_1", "start": 494}, {"end": 1073, "list_id": null, "list_nesting": 0, "named_style": "HEADING_1", "start": 1058}, {"end": 2491, "list_id": null, "list_nesting": 0, "named_style": "HEADING_1", "start": 2479}, {"end": 2731, "list_id": null, "list_nesting": 0, "named_style": "HEADING_1", "start": 2712}, {"end": 3250, "list_id": null, "list_nesting": 0, "named_style": "HEADING_1", "start": 3238}], "title": "[Zombie Ops] Zombie Lane", "visibility": "domain"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gdocs/data.json", "pointer": "/docs_documents/281", "field": "document_id", "value": "f_744027532fb1b0cc8821c4", "record": {"body_text": "Event Icon Management System v1.0\nOverview:\nThe purpose of this system is to create a structure for the LiveOps event icons. This system dictates the following:\nThe number of icons on a scene\nWhen they will appear whether locked or unlocked\nWhat side of the screen will an icon appear\nIn what order an icon will appear\nWhen will the icon disappear and/or change places\nThe various elements on the icon like time, buttons, notifications, etc.\nSeasonal changes\nWhat\u2019s in it for [SOURCE_ORG_0451]:\nTo have an across-prototype transferable Live Operations icon ordering.\nMain Workings:\nIcon Amount\nThe main UI can have a maximum of 10 icons on the screen at any given time.\nIf the situation calls for more icons, both of the columns will shrink in icon size and the slot amount will be increased accordingly.\n(add a  screenshot with different resolutions)\nIcon Placement By Type\nAll gameplay-related icons will be showcased on the left side while the monetization icons will appear on the right.\nIcon Placement By Announcement (Lock State)\nThe event icon management system should have the flexibility to add incoming events by level in a locked state.\nLocked event icons appear semi-grayed out as seen in the image below.\nIf we decide to display lock sprites on top of icons, they will display an unlocking animation when the player hits the corresponding level.\nWhen the player reaches the desired level, the lock does a simple bounce animation before shrinking back to its size and getting color.\nWhile the icons are in their lock state, they shouldn\u2019t get any animations.\nWrite ticket for Marcus to change the lock animation.\nThe graying out will be done with engineering. It will be not be graying out but the black overlay instead. During this operation, we need to consult with the art team and they will dictate the color of the overlay.\nIcon Placement By Order\nMonetization Column\nThe monetization column displays the monetization-related icon with a custom priority. Each icon will have the following attributes:\nSticky\nThis attribute determines whether the icon will remain in the assigned position at all times until the offer is over.\nInitial Starting Position\nEach icon will appear on the screen with an initial starting position. This position is always 1 if There are no sticky icons and the slot after the sticky icons if There are any.\nThis way, any offer will remain sticky for as long as we want it, and all new icons will appear directly under sticky icons. The new icons will naturally take the first slot and others will descend accordingly. So, each time There is a new offer, the icons descend to the next slot.\nGameplay Column\nThe event icon management system will use the following ruleset:\nThe screen displays the locked events (if There are any) to begin with.\nThe screen displays the events as they unlock prioritizing top order.\nAfter all the events have been unlocked, events start queuing.\nThe queue has the following criteria:\nIf the game event icon has a panel that opens and closes it always takes the first place and becomes sticky until the event is over. If a second icon has a panel it takes the second place and follows the same rule.\nThe next priority are the events we tag as sticky.\nAfter that the first try events take their place. They appear in the first slot available when they start and disappear when the event is over.\n5. Icon Elements\nFor the sake of simplicity, each icon will have a ribbon as shown below in the Royal Match example. The text and color of this ribbon will be determined from the code.\nOngoing State (Timer)\nThe ongoing state of an icon means the player has agreed to start the event via pop-up. After that, the icon will display the timer for the event. For auto-start events, the ongoing state starts immediately. \n\nThe timer follows the standard dd:mm:ss format.\nStart State\nThe start state of an icon means the player has ignored the event and didn\u2019t activate it. In that case, the event will display a \u201cStart\u201d text on the ribbon.\nEnd State\nThe end state of an icon is triggered in the following scenarios:\nThe player finished the event but didn\u2019t collect their reward.\nThe player started the event but didn\u2019t finish it.\nLock State\nOnly true if we introduce the icons by level. See above for details.\n*If the players don\u2019t claim rewards and the event cycle resets, it\u2019s better to show a pop-up in case they don\u2019t click on the \u201cclaim\u201d button as well.\nNotification System\nThis system will display different notifications based on the state of the event. The monetization event gets their notifications on the left, whereas the gameplay column gets their notification on the right side of the icon.\nRed Dot Notification\nThe continuation of the red dot notification system we already have.\nGreen Circle Notification\nThe green circle shows uncollected rewards.\nLeaderboard Notification\nLeaderboard notifications are displayed on the icon itself and show the player where they rank within an event.\nDiscount notification\nTo be added to monetization icons as needed.\nProgress System\nThe progress system uses the curved progress bar we currently use in the game. Based on the event, the developer will incorporate the progress bar if stated in the spec-specific event.\n6. Seasonal Changes\nIf we decide to make an event season-based, (e.g. Christmas or Halloween edition) the icon will be updated accordingly. Seasonal event icons follow the same rules as the generic icons.\nArt:\nIcon Skeleton\nThe icons will use a generic frame, similar to what we have in Domino Delights now. Since Domino Delights uses a more fantasy/female-friendly vibe, we might iterate on it. To be discussed further with the art team.\nRank placeholder is not always an option so design around it.\nIconography\nA generic icon library that will be suited for any type of game. All icons will have VFXs that can be grown into other icons as well. So they should be generic. To be discussed with the art team to figure out in the kickoff meeting.\nSo, I did talk with the art team and they ripped me a new one. No generic icons :P\nArt Direction\nGeneral suggestions are listed below:\nSince the notification colors will be white, green, and red, the icons shouldn\u2019t be using these colors heavily.\nAll icons should use a similar/same color scheme to look harmonious no matter what.\nSince the border size and color will be the same, the icons need to follow complimenting borders, thickness, and color.\nThe icons should be 2D elements with 3D perspective. This kind of style is called physical touching (don\u2019t call HR)\nThe ribbons will have the color of the skeleton. (Martin will make a presentation for this)\nWe are a trendy company\nCLAIRE is a Captain Obvious person.\nVFX Consideration\nThe VFXs should be generic and based on manipulation of the shape rather than being icon-specific. To be discussed with the art team whether it\u2019s better to make it code or art-based. \n\nBut for some of the icons, e.g. race flags, we can have them custom made since these icons will be used over multiple prototypes.\nSize change\n[PERSON_NAME_66179]\nBounce\n[USERNAME_12151]\nLock VFX\nThe unlock VFX we currently have should be adjusted to the generic system. See below.\n(low priority) For the ranking events, where the player reaches the top spot, we can add a VFX (TBD) to make it obvious.\nAfter [USERNAME_5509] completes his list and Calvin makes the skeleton prefab, we\u2019ll sync and investigate if adding the generic animations to the prefab makes sense.\nI asked [PERSON_NAME_66177] how long this will take. And he told me to mind my own business. (one week not counting animation work including testing)\nFuture Iterations:\nWe need a system that allows for an event to be unlocked even if it\u2019s not available that day.\nVisual References:", "created_time": "2025-01-10T13:20:25Z", "document_id": "f_744027532fb1b0cc8821c4", "drive_file_id": "f_744027532fb1b0cc8821c4", "modified_time": "2025-07-28T16:54:28Z", "owner_email": "julia.lawson@harmonygames.co", "revision_id": "43e006f2ed", "shared_with_emails": ["marcus.bennett@harmonygames.co", "calvin.price@harmonygames.co"], "style_runs": [{"end": 33, "list_id": null, "list_nesting": 0, "named_style": "HEADING_1", "start": 0}, {"end": 43, "list_id": null, "list_nesting": 0, "named_style": "HEADING_3", "start": 34}, {"end": 191, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 161}, {"end": 240, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 192}, {"end": 284, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 241}, {"end": 318, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 285}, {"end": 368, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 319}, {"end": 441, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 369}, {"end": 458, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 442}, {"end": 494, "list_id": null, "list_nesting": 0, "named_style": "HEADING_3", "start": 459}, {"end": 566, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 495}, {"end": 581, "list_id": null, "list_nesting": 0, "named_style": "HEADING_3", "start": 567}, {"end": 593, "list_id": "list_3", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 582}, {"end": 874, "list_id": "list_3", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 852}, {"end": 1035, "list_id": "list_3", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 992}, {"end": 1217, "list_id": "list_4", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1148}, {"end": 1358, "list_id": "list_4", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1218}, {"end": 1494, "list_id": "list_4", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1359}, {"end": 1570, "list_id": "list_4", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1495}, {"end": 1624, "list_id": "list_4", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1571}, {"end": 1840, "list_id": "list_4", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1625}, {"end": 1864, "list_id": "list_3", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1841}, {"end": 2024, "list_id": "list_5", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 2018}, {"end": 2168, "list_id": "list_5", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 2143}, {"end": 2784, "list_id": "list_6", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 2713}, {"end": 2854, "list_id": "list_6", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 2785}, {"end": 2917, "list_id": "list_6", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 2855}, {"end": 3170, "list_id": "list_7", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 2956}, {"end": 3221, "list_id": "list_7", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 3171}, {"end": 3365, "list_id": "list_7", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 3222}, {"end": 3572, "list_id": "list_8", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 3551}, {"end": 3842, "list_id": "list_8", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 3831}, {"end": 4009, "list_id": "list_8", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 4000}, {"end": 4138, "list_id": "list_9", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 4076}, {"end": 4189, "list_id": "list_9", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 4139}, {"end": 4200, "list_id": "list_8", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 4190}, {"end": 4685, "list_id": "list_10", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 4665}, {"end": 4780, "list_id": "list_10", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 4755}, {"end": 4849, "list_id": "list_10", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 4825}, {"end": 4983, "list_id": "list_10", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 4962}, {"end": 5439, "list_id": null, "list_nesting": 0, "named_style": "HEADING_3", "start": 5435}, {"end": 5453, "list_id": "list_11", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 5440}, {"end": 5730, "list_id": "list_12", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 5669}, {"end": 5742, "list_id": "list_11", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 5731}, {"end": 6072, "list_id": "list_11", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 6059}, {"end": 6222, "list_id": "list_13", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 6111}, {"end": 6306, "list_id": "list_13", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 6223}, {"end": 6426, "list_id": "list_13", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 6307}, {"end": 6542, "list_id": "list_13", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 6427}, {"end": 6634, "list_id": "list_13", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 6543}, {"end": 6658, "list_id": "list_13", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 6635}, {"end": 6712, "list_id": "list_11", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 6695}, {"end": 7039, "list_id": "list_14", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 7028}, {"end": 7059, "list_id": "list_14", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 7040}, {"end": 7066, "list_id": "list_14", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 7060}, {"end": 7083, "list_id": "list_14", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 7067}, {"end": 7299, "list_id": "list_15", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 7179}, {"end": 7465, "list_id": "list_15", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 7300}, {"end": 7615, "list_id": "list_15", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 7466}, {"end": 7634, "list_id": null, "list_nesting": 0, "named_style": "HEADING_3", "start": 7616}, {"end": 7747, "list_id": null, "list_nesting": 0, "named_style": "HEADING_3", "start": 7729}], "title": "[LiveOps] Event Icon Management System", "visibility": "domain"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gdocs/data.json", "pointer": "/docs_documents/315", "field": "document_id", "value": "f_80db8860fb69d86887c2c0", "record": {"body_text": "Layout reference clipboard\nIf we can use this place as a reference clipping board it will be great.\nInstant Play Features.\nBug: Currently, we can\u2019t go back from level preview back to the engine.\nFeature: It\u2019d be great if when we click to \u201cgo back to editor\u201d button, it takes us back to where we left off in the engine.\nThe edit Layout map is different from the real puzzle.\nHandtile Menu Covering puzzle\nCan\u2019t handcode [USERNAME_42354] (doesn\u2019t show correct preview)\nMirrored prefabs are distorted.\nAlign Tool Upgrade\n(not sure tbd later)\n[USERNAME_60760]\nBlue tile alignment dots are sometimes lines, and sometimes really big dots. It\u2019d be great if we could stabilize this. \n\nNote: Since alignment works fine, this is not a huge priority now.\nNotes: I\u2019m not sure why this happens and I can\u2019t reproduce what triggers it. But when it happens tile alignment won\u2019t work, I hope that\u2019s a good enough clue.\nRandom layouts like [USERNAME_9170] won't accept changes. I can always delete them manually and it's not that big an issue, but when fixing alignment etc, we want to be sure changes are registering so I was hoping you could take a look.\nhttps://harmonygamesgroup.Slack.com/files/U05GU6KV231/F065FB5LJAK/ekran_kayd___2023-11-15_18.36.57.mov\nIf a layout has too many generations, I can't hit play or simulate. It's not essential, can live without it for alpha, just sending it in case you know a quick fix to it.\nhttps://harmonygamesgroup.Slack.com/files/U05GU6KV231/F066JSRV1L0/ekran_kayd___2023-11-15_18.40.18.mov\nUI Borders\nWe kind of forgot about this but, please give me some UI mock-up or just borders to help me not step over the UI or not leave too much space.\nPrefab Library\nIt would be great to have an Approved Prefab library like Approved Layouts given we\u2019ll soon have lots of prefabs.\n\nNext step: Prefabs disappear when I exit the play mode. It would be nice to save them to create the library\nIn that vein,\nI\u2019ll probably name prefabs by their shape (curve, line, etc.) So if I\u2019m looking for a curvy prefab and I search by name to eliminate the rest of the prefabs, that\u2019ll be awesome. Can work with a tagging system too if that\u2019s easier.\nChoosing rotation angle\nCurrently, the rotation tool uses increments of 15 or manual. I love manual but it\u2019s hard to get the exact number. It would be great to either just type the number in.\nNext step: This works, but sometimes it resets to a 15 degree increment and I have to do it twice. (before you ask, yes I do press enter \ud83d\ude00)\nNevermind I\u2019m stupid. When I hit \u201c1\u201d it goes to rotate as a hot key, that\u2019s the problem I was having. Can we change the 1 hot key to something else? The qwert row is ok with me.\nSelection/Layering Bug\nSelecting a group of tiles may change it\u2019s layering. Mostly happens with curve patterns but occasionally happens with vertical and horizontal shapes as well.\nStill happens with old prefabs and layouts but I guess we can cross this out?\nWhen selected (normal)\nWhen released (layer bug)\nAdvanced Tiles\nWe need the other advanced tiles built into the editor at your earliest convenience so that we can add them to test levels and playtest them.\nRotate Selection\nPurely for aesthetics, no real need at all. Nice to have. Total luxury. Not a luxury anymore, I need this to help me with the changing camera angle.\nWhen regular rotation tool is used.\nWhen selection rotation is used\nInstant Play Return\nInstant play works great, but once I hit it I have nowhere to come back to the editor. Can be added to the settings icon too, whatever\u2019s easiest.\nPreview bug\nHappens at random.\nHappens everywhere a preview is used.\nHappens more often when the longer play mode is running.\nIt overwrites a random prefab all level onto the correct display. See photos down below.\nNormal Look\nDistorted Look\nNormal Look\nDistorted Look\nAlignment Bug - AKA the gift that keeps on giving\nSee video on the engineering channel.\nhttps://harmonygamesgroup.Slack.com/archives/C050WGU41HR/p1697828447764129\nAccess to layout editing\nIf double-clicking the image could send me to the edit mode of that layout that\u2019d be a lifesaver! Otherwise, I\u2019m scrolling down tens of layouts to find the exact match.\nSimplifying layout search\nIt\u2019d be great if I could search for a layout by name.\nSpawn Point\nCan we have a new tile not spawn in the middle? When I just need to make one little adjustment, having it spawn in the middle is a pain.", "created_time": "2023-10-20T16:39:24Z", "document_id": "f_80db8860fb69d86887c2c0", "drive_file_id": "f_80db8860fb69d86887c2c0", "modified_time": "2024-02-26T19:03:19Z", "owner_email": "julia.lawson@harmonygames.co", "revision_id": "bcf6bc8f32", "shared_with_emails": [], "style_runs": [{"end": 26, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 0}, {"end": 122, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 100}, {"end": 373, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 319}, {"end": 403, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 374}, {"end": 466, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 404}, {"end": 498, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 467}, {"end": 517, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 499}, {"end": 555, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 539}, {"end": 1138, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 902}, {"end": 1412, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1242}, {"end": 1526, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1516}, {"end": 1683, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1669}, {"end": 2175, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 2152}, {"end": 2684, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 2662}, {"end": 2984, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 2970}, {"end": 3143, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 3127}, {"end": 3380, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 3361}, {"end": 3538, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 3527}, {"end": 3845, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 3796}, {"end": 3983, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 3959}, {"end": 4178, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 4153}, {"end": 4244, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 4233}], "title": "Puzzle Engine Wishlist_", "visibility": "private"}}], "records_checked": 633, "files_selected": 1, "files_completed": 1, "scan_complete": true, "errors": []}}, "files_read_this_call": 2, "sources": [{"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gdocs/data.json", "manifest_sha256": "01005ffefe422717f27a5c3f7820c426dc7a3f15b30fa2c959bbb2acaab1dd2d", "freshness": "55ea7b8ba40ec0fdca868d3538a91844b79ea64f0e4dc0c053af849cadcef3cc"}], "scan_complete": true, "persona_filtered": false, "backend": "grouped-record-scan", "scope_note": "Exact direct fields in selected arrays. No SQL is applied. Absence/uniqueness is supported only within complete declared scopes. Manifest hashes are declared provenance, not fresh full-content hashes."}, "checksum": "a110eb8f40f93f6fb97ddba03cd3baf944efd38cd8fc7c5282e25fb128e9ee1f"}